// OWNER: land. Layers L-shore (0.6), L-roadside (0.9), L-road (1.0), L-foreground (1.3).
// Style B (docs/STYLE-B.md): a warm storybook-gouache seafront. Every prop is a painted picture-book object: warm
// gouache paints (the `materials` below + the time-of-day env tokens, so the whole page is graded by the hour), a
// warm-brown hand-drawn ink line (thinner and softer on the far beach, bolder in the foreground = atmospheric
// perspective), seeded wobble baked into every outline, a second offset "pencil" pass on the bigger props, tapered
// brush dabs for light and shade, and static gouache <pattern> textures (sand speckle, dry brush, wood grain, grass,
// flagstones) in each object's own local coordinates. NO filters anywhere (STYLE-B §2): these layers stream and
// recycle, so the hand-made look is geometry, identical every frame.
//
// Design coordinates = the hero frame (t = 3.2 s at 60 rpm): every object is drawn where it sits on screen in that
// frame. Each near layer = (a) a BASE tile of the continuous surfaces tiled by 3 <use> copies; (b) the hand-composed
// hero village tile shown once per lap; (c) a pooled STREAM of <use> props keyed by absolute prop index (seeded
// choice / flip / scale / paint swap per stretch of the route, so the ≥ 4-minute lap never repeats); (d) unique SET
// PIECES (pier, harbour, pleasure pier, railway + racing train, lighthouse point, cliffs, bridge, fort & lido …)
// mounted on approach. Per frame: transforms only, plus href swaps when a pool slot recycles (no DOM churn).
